WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
Speaker 1: We're starting today with a story that&nbsp;
comes to us from the the poorest country in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:14.720
Western Hemisphere, the country of Haiti, where&nbsp;
the Haitian president was assassinated in his home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.560
early yesterday morning. The New York Times&nbsp;
has a very good article summing this up called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:28.000
Haiti's president assassinated in a nighttime raid&nbsp;
shaking a fragile nation. A group of assailants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.000
stormed Mr. Moises residence early on Wednesday,&nbsp;
shooting him and wounding his wife. The interim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.840
prime minister declaring a state of siege. The&nbsp;
first explosions took place around 1:00 a.m.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:52.960
and this took place at the home of President Jovan&nbsp;
Elmore's. And this is a wealthy neighborhood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.680
Residents immediately feared two of the terrors&nbsp;
that have plagued the nation, gang violence or an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:06.640
earthquake. But by the morning, they had learned&nbsp;
that the president was dead. A group of assailants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.840
had stormed Mr. Mozes residency on the outskirts&nbsp;
of the capital, Port au Prince, early Wednesday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:18.640
shooting him and wounding his wife. Martine was&nbsp;
in what officials called a well planned operation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.080
that included foreigners who spoke Spanish.&nbsp;
Much is being made of the Spanish aspect of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.960
although it's really too early to know too much&nbsp;
about what that means. In a televised broadcast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.520
to the nation, the nation's interim prime&nbsp;
minister, Claude Joseph, appealed for calm and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.600
presented himself as the new head of government,&nbsp;
announcing that he and his fellow ministers had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:44.480
declared a state of siege and placed Haiti under&nbsp;
a form of martial law. The assassination left a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:49.040
political void that deepened the turmoil and&nbsp;
violence that has gripped Haiti for months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.520
threatening to tip one of the world's most&nbsp;
troubled nations further into lawlessness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.360
You know, I'm not sure how much people in the&nbsp;
audience know about the history of Haiti. Haiti&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:06.160
is on a landmass that is an island that is shared&nbsp;
with another country, the Dominican Republic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.040
Haiti in the east and the Dominican Republic&nbsp;
I'm sorry, Haiti in the west and the Dominican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:17.200
Republic to the east. The island is called&nbsp;
Espanola. And there are really, really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:25.200
racist, crude, quote, explanations that are&nbsp;
given for why. OK, the Dominican Republic is&nbsp;&nbsp;

